    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) is the clear anchor of the Austin Waves lineup. His matchup against the right-handed Alcantara is prime territory for a massive output, bolstered by an 11% boost from the pitcher's efficiency rating and a significant 14% dynamic platoon advantage. Alongside him, **Josh Lowe** (72.21) and **Nolan Schanuel** (69.91) are high-ceiling plays; both benefit from the favorable xERA of Erick Fedde and are aided by wind-out conditions at the park, making them essential pivots for our offensive floor. While **Heliot Ramos** (66.80) and **Miguel Vargas** (66.33) carry strong scores, note that both are reliant on the presumed lineup spots; any shift in order could dampen their run-scoring potential.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Marcell Ozuna** (61.28), who sits just outside the active roster despite a solid score. Ultimately, the optimizer prioritized the positional flexibility and dynamic platoon edges offered by **Miguel Vargas** and **Josh Jung** (65.63), whose matchup against the vulnerable 7.06 xERA of Elmer Rodr\u00edguez was simply too enticing to pass up. While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (52.08) remains a high-pedigree asset, the combination of a tougher matchup against Rasmussen and a regression in his base projection keeps him on the pine. As a reminder, the heavy reliance on \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions\u2014specifically for **Drake Baldwin** and **Kyle Tucker**\u2014introduces non-trivial volatility; should these players slide down in the order upon official release, their utility as speed or power contributors may see a slight downward revision in daily efficiency.",
